{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA1129558","title":"Methanogenic limonene-degrading enrichment culture","description":"Limonene, a monocyclic monoterpene, is present in human environments, in food, and as a citrus scent in cosmetics and cleaning products. It enters wastewater and is anoxically transformed and degraded in methanogenic digester towers. In this study, the PacBio metagenome of a stable limonene-degrading methanogenic enrichment culture was used to characterize the microbial community and identify the degradation pathway of limonene.","center":"Max Planck Institute for Marine Microbiology","data_type":"Genome sequencing","submission_date":"2024/06/28 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN42232246","Metagenome or environmental sample from activated sludge metagenome","confirmed_urban","municipal_wastewater",null,1997,"DE","Lower Saxony",2856500,"Osterholz-Scharmbeck","verified",53.2111,8.7894,"Germany: Lintel, Osterholz-Scharmbeck","activated sludge from anaerobic digester, wastewater treatment plant",null,null,null,"named urban infrastructure at sample level"],["SAMN42623487","Metagenome or environmental sample from activated sludge metagenome","confirmed_urban","municipal_wastewater",null,1997,"DE","Lower Saxony",2856500,"Osterholz-Scharmbeck","verified",53.2111,8.7894,"Germany: Lintel, Osterholz-Scharmbeck","activated sludge from anaerobic digester, wastewater treatment plant",null,null,null,"named urban infrastructure at sample level"],["SAMN42623570","Metagenome or environmental sample from activated sludge metagenome","confirmed_urban","municipal_wastewater",null,1997,"DE","Lower Saxony",2856500,"Osterholz-Scharmbeck","verified",53.2111,8.7894,"Germany: Lintel, Osterholz-Scharmbeck","activated sludge from anae